2. what is Inferschema in spark?
=> In Apache Spark, inferSchema is an option used when reading data—especially from CSV or 
  JSON files—to automatically detect the data types of columns instead of treating everything as strings.
=> df = spark.read.option("header", "true").option("inferSchema", "true").csv("path/to/data.csv")
=> By default, Spark reads all columns as strings (StringType)
=> root
 |-- id: string
 |-- name: string
 |-- age: string
 |-- salary: string
=> With inferSchema:
df = spark.read.option("header", "true").option("inferSchema", "true").csv("data.csv")
df.printSchema()
=> root
 |-- id: integer
 |-- name: string
 |-- age: integer
 |-- salary: double

=> Best Practices
    inferSchema is handy for small datasets or exploration.
    For production or large datasets, explicitly defining schemas is safer and faster.
    Inferring schema can slow down the read for large files since Spark must scan data.
